  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 248 PM EDT Thu Jul 23 2026\n\n- Dry through Saturday morning\n\nHigh pressure will dominate the area weather tonight through\nSaturday morning. Vertical profiles show a distinct lack of\nmoisture through that time outside of some occasional cumulus\nlevel moisture. We are looking at mostly clear to partly cloudy\nconditions through Saturday morning. Lows in the 50s and highs\naround 80 will be common through Saturday.\n\n- Periods of showers/storms possible Saturday night into Tuesday\n\nThe first question during this period is when do showers and\nthunderstorms first make it back into the forecast. It still\nappears to be Saturday night, but there is a push of moisture and\ntherefore MUCAPE into Southwest Lower Michigan Saturday afternoon\nand evening. The NAM is more bullish on this, but even the ECMWF\nand GFS have MUCAPE values into the 500-1000 j/kg range. PWATs\nsurge to 1.5+ inches during the same time. We will be watching\nthis time frame closely as many have summer activities going on. \n\nThe pattern from Saturday night through Tuesday is dominated by\nnorthwest upper flow between a Plains ridge and a low centered\nnear Hudson Bay much of the time. Low level moisture will be back\nin place which will make periodic thunderstorms possible each\nforecast period. Trying to nail down the more likely periods for\nshowers and storms is the challenge. The two main focus periods\nare Sunday afternoon and evening and again Monday afternoon and\nevening. The upper shortwaves are subtle but it appears the Monday\nwave may be the stronger one. The ECWMF with the Monday wave\nproduces a fairly deep surface low, sweeping a 994mb low through\nthe Great Lakes. Mid level flow surges above 50 knots at times as\nwell. So, at this point it looks likely that we will see periodic\nstorms during this period with the threat of severe weather as\nwell. Sunday and Monday would be the two highest likelihood days\nfor the potential of strong to severe storms. Locally heavy rain\nwill be possible as well given mid summer moisture in place. \n\n- Temperatures warming into Sunday/Monday\n\nTemperatures will warm from around 80 today and Friday to around\n90 Sunday into Monday. 850mb temperatures warm to around +22C on\nMonday. The warm temperatures will combine with summer moisture to\nproduce max apparent temperatures into the 90s. The highest\napparent temperatures surge to 98 in the southeast CWA near\nJackson on Monday.",
